Requirements: 6   with obligations: 6

[task-01] When the review builds an edit for a named plausible defect, it asks for
    several candidate edits instead of one and uses the first that passes the checks the
    review already applies to an edit. How many candidates it asks for is configurable.
    When no candidate passes, the review says that none of the candidates it asked for
    could be used, rather than that the defect cannot be turned into an edit, and
    otherwise handles the defect the way it handles one no edit could be built for
    today.
    -> multiple-candidate-edits  [functional/explicit]
       The review asks for several candidate edits instead of one.
    -> first-passing-candidate  [functional/explicit]
       Use the first candidate edit that passes the checks the review already applies to
       an edit.
    -> candidate-count-configurable  [docs_config/explicit]
       The number of candidates the review asks for is configurable.
    -> none-of-candidates-could-be-used  [functional/explicit]
       When no candidate passes, the review says that none of the candidates it asked
       for could be used.
    -> preserve-no-edit-built-fallback-handling  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the review's handling of a defect when no edit could be built for today.

[task-02] For each defect, the review records how many candidates it asked for, how many
    it set aside and why, and which candidate it used. Its report says what building
    edits cost and how long it took, since asking for several candidates multiplies
    both.
    -> candidate-count-recorded  [functional/explicit]
       The review records how many candidates it asked for.
    -> set-aside-count-and-reasons  [functional/explicit]
       Record how many candidates were set aside and why.
    -> which-candidate-it-used  [functional/explicit]
       Record which candidate it used for each defect review.
    -> report-build-edit-cost-and-duration  [functional/explicit]
       The report states what building edits cost and how long they took.

[constraint-01] Two runs over the same input pick the same candidate.
    -> deterministic-candidate-selection  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over the same input pick the same candidate.

[exclusion-01] Whether an edit that passes the checks really makes its named defect
    true.
    -> edit-passes-checks-defect-true  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether an edit that passes the checks really makes its
       named defect true.

[exclusion-02] Which plausible defects are enumerated, and which region of the code an
    edit is allowed to fall in.
    -> exclude-plausible-defects-and-region  [docs_config/explicit]
       The change does not alter which plausible defects are enumerated or which region
       of the code an edit is allowed to fall in.

[exclusion-03] Which tests are candidates, how the project's tests are run, and how the
    result of a run is read.
    -> exclude-test-candidate-selection-and-run-flow  [docs_config/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are candidates, how the project's tests are
       run, or how the result of a run is read.

